{"name":"Sugarloaf Brown","hex":"#554400","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sugarloaf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of sugar-loaf."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sugarloaf"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sugarloaf","blocks":[{"text":"A sugarloaf was the usual form in which refined sugar was produced and sold until the late 19th century, when granulated and cube sugars were introduced. A tall cone with a rounded top was the end product of a process in which dark molasses, a rich raw sugar that was imported from sugar-growing regions, such as the Caribbean and Brazil, was refined into white sugar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Cukrov%C3%A1_homole_001.jpg/330px-Cukrov%C3%A1_homole_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugarloaf"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Sugar_cones_-b.jpg/120px-Sugar_cones_-b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Sugar_cones_-b.jpg/250px-Sugar_cones_-b.jp